+## Selection and remaining limits
+
+`task-2-specimen-candidates.json` proposes nine actual-child URLs: quarterly ZIP bodies for 2010Q1, 2015Q1, 2015Q4, 2016Q1, 2026Q3 and 2026Q4; root ZIP for the current-root/year-QTR relationship; and daily IDX bodies for 2026-10-01 and 2026-10-02. These cover intended/development boundaries, year transition, latest closed/open quarter, root relationship, handoff and published daily source within the 12-specimen cap. Root makes the actual Task 3 selection. Root clarified that its final matrix will cover daily year and quarter transitions, using actual retained daily entries for 2025-12-31/2026-01-02 and 2026-09-30/2026-10-01, with the handoff role reused. The additional actual-child references are in `task-2-daily-transition-advisory.json`; the earlier proposed quarterly transition specimens are advisory and may be omitted. Only Task 3 selects the final matrix.
+
+The proposed selected families are quarterly ZIP and uncompressed daily IDX. `.gz`, `.Z`, `.z`, `.sit` and other daily archive alternatives are optional listed representations, unselected and unexamined. They do not imply codec support or require speculative downloads when the selected alternative covers the source. Novelty detection is a manual root review control: the helper has no automated format-family novelty detector, and the offline checks do not claim to test one. The newly observed .sit/.z names are unselected optional archive-codec alternatives within the known master-index source family; no body was inspected, so a new selected content family has not been established. Root has paused further SEC requests pending this checkpoint review. If chosen body inspection reveals a new content format, legacy row/path family or requires expanded sampling, root must stop and coordinate explicit additional window/review authorization; this task grants no expanded sampling budget. No codec, text encoding, line ending, archive content or legacy path/accession support is asserted here.
+
+SEC documentation received as SEC-0140 describes weekly rebuilding of quarterly/full indexes and the current-quarter full-index bridge through the previous business day. It describes daily files through the current year. That wording does not pin an oldest retained year or guarantee arbitrary historical outage recovery; observed 2010–2026 directories are separate receipt-time source observations. There is no necessary contradiction between “through current year” and historic directory presence. Neither the bridge description nor similar representation names establishes byte equality of root and year/QTR bodies; Task 3 must compare actual originals.
+
+D-14 records the 33 uninspected historical daily middle quarters. Before asserting recovery spanning them, inspect relevant additional directories in another accepted bounded window or obtain explicit owner gap/contract resolution. No range revision has been inferred or accepted. Existing readiness/runtime decisions remain root-owned. Open-quarter availability is sensitive to this receipt date and must be reevaluated on later runs.
